Joaquin:

There are many factors that affect detectability, many of which exhibit temporal variability.  Examples include:

time of day surveys are conducted (song rate changes over the course of a day, or morning), alertness of observer (some days I am more awake than other days), weather conditions (wind and rain can influence animal behaviour as well as observer ability to detect song bursts).

